// CONTRACTS optimized
// EXPECT_STDOUT PROVEN_ELIDED_OPTIMIZED_OK
// EXPECT_EXIT_CODE 0
//
// Plan 194 A2.1 (retires Plan 140 Ф.2 / D24-amend `--contracts=off`):
// this fixture historically exercised the legacy build-policy `off`
// (global unconditional elision of ALL contract checks — unsound for
// unproven contracts). Atom A2.1 removes `off` entirely: `checked` /
// `optimized` / `verified` all enforce unproven contracts (no global
// bypass survives under any flag value — see emit_c.rs
// `contracts_elided_for`), so the original "unproven requires silently
// skipped, exit 0" scenario can no longer be expressed.
//
// Repurposed per the A2.1 migration note (map item 5): cover "under
// `optimized`, a genuinely PROVEN contract is still elided (zero-cost)"
// — the direct analogue of `t2_proven_elided.nv`'s `enforce`/`checked`
// case, but exercised through the `optimized` flag value. In THIS atom
// `optimized` is byte-identical to `checked` (see `ContractsMode` doc in
// compiler-codegen/src/ast/mod.rs); differentiated Z3-driven elision
// specifically under `optimized`/`verified` is future work (atoms
// A2.2+/A3, волна 2).

module standalone.t5_build_policy_off
fn must_be_positive(x int) -> int
    requires x > 0
    ensures result > 0
=> x * 2

fn main() Io -> () {
    // x=5 SATISFIES `requires x > 0`; `ensures result > 0` is statically
    // PROVABLE from it (x>0 ⟹ x*2>0) — both TrivialBackend and Z3 discharge
    // this VC, so it lands in `proven_contracts` and is elided at codegen
    // even under `--contracts=optimized`.
    ro r = must_be_positive(5)
    if r == 10 {
        println("PROVEN_ELIDED_OPTIMIZED_OK")
    } else {
        println("UNEXPECTED")
    }
}
